==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Necromancer Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Necro-Dancer Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Although able to communicate with the supernatural, Shaman Cat has a more useful skill in its ability to freeze [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies. However due to his somewhat short range in his 1st and 2nd forms, it may be difficult to use him properly against Floating enemies, especially the ones that outrange him. Alongside this, his attack rate is much worse than other reliable crowd-controllers, like Bishop Cat.

His best targets include [[Shy Boy]], most [[Teacher Bun Bun]] variants, [[Red Cyclone]], [[Dark Cyclone]] and [[White Cyclone]].

Aside from his anti-Floating abilities, Necromancer Cat is included in the [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] [[Cat Combo]], which can be combined with [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] for a research power boost, which greatly helps for units like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]].

==='''True Form'''===
Necro-Dancer Cat has a much better range, increasing the distance between him and the enemies, thereby making him easier to stack. Sadly, he is still outranged by many Floating enemies, like [[Owlbrow]] and [[Mooth]], which means that this shouldn't be your go-to cat when facing Floating enemies, but he is still helpful.

Since he only has a 20% chance to freeze Floating enemies and Single Attack, one or two Necro-Dancer Cats should never be relied on as your only defense against them; instead stack more, like 6~8 as then they will be much more reliable. When provided support from other anti-Floating Cats like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], Necro-Dancer may be able to be the final nail in the coffin for them, completely freezing Floating enemies when stacked enough. This is notable in the fight against [[Mecha-Bun (Enemy)|Mecha-Bun]] in [[Eldritch Forces]], as he outranges Mecha-Bun's Omni Strike by 60 and and can completely paralyze it.

==='''Talents'''===
His Wave Attack [[Talents]] give him a pseudo-Area Attack and enables him to reach Owlbrow and Mooth variants behind the frontlines. Since the Freeze and Wave Attack abilities each have a separate, small chance to activate, the probability of both abilities triggering on a single attack (resulting in a freezing wave) is a mere 6%, meaning that a massive stack is needed to make full use of this Talent. Because of this, Sanzo Cat is still usually the better option against groups of Floating enemies; but as before, when stacked enough to create consistent waves, Necro-Dancer may even outperform Sanzo.

His [[Immune to Toxic]] talent allows him to become a counter for [[Gobble]], which is important for late-game players, although his low health makes it less effective than [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]] with the same talent, in that case. Other talents do not improve this unit in any relevant way, so they should be avoided.

==='''Orb'''===
The only Effect Orb with any effect would be health up vs Floating, as it may allow this Cat to take one more hit from certain sources. Death Mini-Surge could provide insurance for your stack of Necro-Dancers dying. Still, the limited need for this cat, combined with the low health, makes using an orb on him hardly worth it.

