==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.6 Update|Version 2.0.6]] increased Shaman Cat's freeze chance from 10% to 20%.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Shaman Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Medium Cool (Removed Combo)|Medium Cool]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Shaman Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Shaman Cat
Able to communicate with the supernatural.
… is what it says on the Wiki.
Might freeze Floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Necromancer Cat
Turns out it was the supernatural that was
controlling this Cat in the end.
Might freeze Floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Necro-Dancer Cat
His bewitching dance is fueled by dark
powers. Can you resist his devilish groove?
Might freeze Floating enemies for longer.</pre>
*Shaman Cat gets its name from a [[wikipedia:Shamanism|shaman]]—someone who can make contact with supernatural beings.
*Necromancer Cat's Japanese name, Nekoramansā (ネコラマンサー), is a pun on necromancer, which is someone who communicates with the dead.
*Necro-Dancer Cat is a possible reference to the Necrodancer from the video game ''[[wikipedia:Crypt of the NecroDancer|Crypt of the NecroDancer]]''. Its description also refers to how the Necrodancer's magic causes the dead as well as those he afflicts to come to life and dance.
*One of the possible [[Cat Shrine#Cat Fortune|Cat Fortunes]] is "Shaman Cat has the perfect cure for your ills."

